# Air-unit camera video options. Sourced by /etc/init.d/ml-air-camera.
#
# BITRATE is the per-tile encoder bitrate in bits per second, and there are two tiles, so the
# link carries twice this. Empty leaves ml-air-video on its own default of 4000000, which is half
# the vendor's 8000 kbps no-link total and the value every camera-to-goggle run so far was
# measured at.
#
# This is the session's bitrate when /etc/conf.d/ml-air-link has RATE_MODE=fixed. Under
# RATE_MODE=adapt it is only the value the encoder opens with: the first MCS sample replaces it,
# and the link owns it from then on.
BITRATE=
